    narr:narration """A cutover-planning call, run in order. [Tanya opens under steering-group pressure to decide the cutover shape](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_1), and [Tina lays out the four sites, flagging the one nobody wants to touch](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5). [Tanya states her settled position: one site at a time, soak between sites, no parallel cutovers](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8). [Xavier pushes back on the shared dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), which [Tanya answers with the contained-versus-unbounded trade](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13) and [Tina reinforces](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15). [Tina then pins the soak to two full weeks](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17), grounded in [the Dockside exception curve from the spring pilot](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19), which [Xavier notes is the only evidence on the table](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_21). [Xavier's replica rule — reporting never touches live during cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_26) is accepted with [the four-minute-staleness trade-off](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_28) and [Tanya making it a runbook rule, not guidance](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_31). Finally [Xavier's reference-data position — vendor stays system of record until the last site is green](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36), with [Tanya adding the vendor-accountability angle](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_39). [Tanya closes with the four-point summary for the steering group](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_42).""" ;
